                        "entry_id": "0a9a0138-adba-35da-b60d-736b365c0daf",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The degree or property of being masculine or manly; manliness."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable",
                            "usually"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1a3a3e79-9c47-4558-947e-361629d8ed2c",
                                "sense_id": "d927f77f-8233-3076-990c-74955e1a690a",
                                "text": "Over time, society's ideas of masculinity has greatly broadened."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c542a446-c087-4d4a-8a50-c2b854b05000",
                                "sense_id": "d927f77f-8233-3076-990c-74955e1a690a",
                                "text": "Of the six homosexual patients, three men finally overcame the underlying vaginaphobia, increased their heterosexual activities, and enhanced their masculinity."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8ca452d3-0df8-4fc9-870a-2b05a20c19b5",
                                "sense_id": "d927f77f-8233-3076-990c-74955e1a690a",
                                "text": "Steven Cohan highlights the suggestive qualities of Red Rivers dominant narrative, the opposition between the radically different masculinities Clift and Wayne represent: \"the highly charged context between the soft boy and the hard man in '''Red River dramatizes such a shift in the mainstream culture's demands upon ''masculinity\"."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
